<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sholoi Setsen Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sholoi Setsen Khan was the first ruler of the Setsen Khanate, one of the khanates of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalkha-mongols">Khalkha Mongols</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, in the first half of the 17th century. As the khanate lay nearest to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>, he exchanged embassies and sent tribute to the rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> state of the Later Jin and the early Qing, while sometimes clashing with them over raids.</p></div>
